      "owner_directive": "Precedence decision from owner: project > user > package > core (owner's UI per-target tier choice is deferred to follow-up issue 2049). User-tier discovery loads unconditionally like types; manifest defaults stay project-only. Previewers become the third consumer of core/dropins.py: scoped sys.path via prepended_sys_paths, collision guard generalized to previewer dirs, bytecode eviction, BaseException isolation, failures recorded on registry diagnostics; render-time lazy string providers re-activate previewer import roots like BlockRegistry.instantiate does. The live work-import brief template carried the same stale no-user-tier instruction and was re-transcribed per FR-026.",
